{"run": "digest", "t": 33426, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] Ethiopian civil conflict, Persecution of Christians in Ethiopia — The Ethiopian Orthodox Tewahedo Church reports that at least 60 Christians have been killed in attacks in Oromia, Ethiopia, over the last week."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 33426, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] Nigerian bandit conflict — The casualty toll from the massacre by unknown gunmen four days ago in Taraba State, Nigeria, increases to 62 people killed and 52 more wounded."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 33426, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] United States strikes on alleged drug traffickers during Operation Southern Spear — The United States launches an airstrike against an alleged drug boat in the Caribbean Sea, killing five people."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 33426, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] Colombian conflict — A bomb explodes near a bridge in Cúcuta, Colombia, at the border with Venezuela, injuring four police officers."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 33426, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Arts and culture] Eurovision Song Contest 2027 — Netherlands Public Broadcasting (NPO) withdraws the Netherlands from the 2027 Eurovision Song Contest over concerns about Israel's participation, after AVROTROS withdrew in August and NPO failed to find another broadcaster."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 33426, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Disasters and accidents] Four people are killed, two are missing and several homes are destroyed during floods in Haiti and the Dominican Republic."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 33426, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Disasters and accidents] A construction site is hit by a tornado in Kepez, Antalya, Turkey, killing four workers and injuring another."}
